  "limitations": [
    "The skill cannot provide cancellation, transactionality, locking, signatures, or idempotency when the runtime/target does not expose those primitives.",
    "Approval binding is structurally hardened by a canonical digest captured outside the executor-editable contract; cryptographic authenticity still depends on the host runtime preserving that root approval receipt.",
    "Deterministic semantic checks reject known contradictions but cannot prove arbitrary real-world claims such as whether true parallelism actually exists; root semantic preflight remains required.",
    "Behavioral activation remains instruction-driven. The included observation grader can score captured contracts, but isolated stochastic runtime trials require host support.",
    "Irreversible/high-consequence actions are intentionally outside the autonomous envelope.",
    "External-write preauthorization is bound to a root-supplied reference by the bundled validators; authenticity still depends on the host preserving the root receipt rather than allowing executor-controlled substitution.",
    "User-visible progress is enforceable only at boundaries where the host runtime allows the root to emit output; blocking tools/harnesses may prevent mid-operation messages, so the skill reports at the next available boundary and never claims unsupported live progress."
  ]
}
